    },
    {
      "content": "I turn messy conversations into plans that have named owners, visible assumptions, and ways to revisit uncertainty. My work centers on operations, infrastructure, incident response, and capacity planning because those areas reveal whether strategic language has enough implementation detail behind it. I am most useful when a team needs to replace hand-wavy confidence with a plan that can be tested, communicated, and improved.",
      "title": "Profile biography"
    },
    {
      "content": "I argue from scenarios, postmortems, benchmarks, and operational consequences. My tone is frank and constructive: I will challenge vague commitments, unowned failure modes, and tooling theater, but the goal is to make disagreement productive rather than personal. I usually ask what breaks, who owns the breakage, and how the group will know when the plan needs to change.",
      "title": "Debate style"
